1
00:01:20,440 --> 00:01:22,120
Think nothing of this.

2
00:01:23,200 --> 00:01:24,240
Yau You-fong!

3
00:01:26,200 --> 00:01:27,080
Where's my daughter?

4
00:01:27,160 --> 00:01:28,560
Where's my daughter?

5
00:01:28,640 --> 00:01:30,000
Who are you? Who's your daughter?

6
00:01:30,080 --> 00:01:32,760
My daughter is Sylvia. She's missing.

7
00:01:32,840 --> 00:01:35,520
Says who? Can you prove you're her father?

8
00:01:38,520 --> 00:01:39,240
Look!

9
00:01:39,320 --> 00:01:40,600
Happy birthday, Honey!

10
00:01:40,680 --> 00:01:41,600
Stop filming, Pops!

11
00:01:41,680 --> 00:01:43,520
Just smile...hurry up!

12
00:01:43,640 --> 00:01:45,680
I've been looking for her for a week.

13
00:01:45,760 --> 00:01:47,200
I called her Mom in Taiwan.

14
00:01:47,320 --> 00:01:48,560
She doesn't know where she is.

15
00:01:48,680 --> 00:01:49,760
Tell me where she is.

16
00:01:49,920 --> 00:01:51,160
I'm looking for her too.

17
00:01:51,440 --> 00:01:52,760
Quit your act!

18
00:01:52,880 --> 00:01:54,840
I know you post your PDA online.

19
00:01:54,960 --> 00:01:56,880
She told me you're her boyfriend

20
00:01:57,000 --> 00:01:58,800
and you lied to her.

21
00:01:58,920 --> 00:02:00,960
I caught you with another girl.

22
00:02:01,080 --> 00:02:02,080
Don't bother to deny it.

23
00:02:02,240 --> 00:02:04,000
Calm down. This is my ex-wife.

24
00:02:04,160 --> 00:02:05,760
Rekindling an old flame?

25
00:02:05,840 --> 00:02:07,600
What have you done to my daughter?

26
00:02:07,720 --> 00:02:09,440
I didn't do anything.

27
00:02:10,160 --> 00:02:13,280
Look what she did to us.

28
00:02:14,760 --> 00:02:15,600
Why should I believe you?

29
00:02:15,680 --> 00:02:17,160
How would I know she did this?

30
00:02:18,040 --> 00:02:18,800
Look!

31
00:02:18,880 --> 00:02:21,760
She's mad at Davis because of me.

32
00:02:21,840 --> 00:02:23,600
That's why she took it out on me.

33
00:02:23,680 --> 00:02:25,760
If I didn't recognize the place and
arrived just in time,

34
00:02:25,840 --> 00:02:27,440
Angie could have died.

35
00:02:27,560 --> 00:02:28,880
My daughter is not ruthless.

36
00:02:29,120 --> 00:02:30,400
What exactly happened?

37
00:02:30,520 --> 00:02:32,880
She moved out and didn't tell me where to.

38
00:02:33,040 --> 00:02:34,160
You must know where she is.

39
00:02:34,280 --> 00:02:36,880
I can take you to her studio.

40
00:02:37,640 --> 00:02:39,280
I'll go with you.

41
00:02:39,360 --> 00:02:41,200
After what happened,
you should get some rest.

42
00:02:41,320 --> 00:02:42,480
I'll call you.

43
00:02:42,600 --> 00:02:43,720
Be careful!

44
00:02:44,800 --> 00:02:46,000
Let's go.

45
00:02:48,600 --> 00:02:51,360
Sylvia, open up! I brought your Dad!

46
00:02:51,520 --> 00:02:54,000
Honey, it's me. Open up!

47
00:02:55,840 --> 00:02:58,560
Don't you have the code?

48
00:02:58,680 --> 00:03:01,920
It was 1111, but she changed it.

49
00:03:13,200 --> 00:03:15,200
Here, she has this habit...

50
00:03:15,280 --> 00:03:17,200
She's worried she'll forget the code

51
00:03:17,320 --> 00:03:18,840
or forget the key.

52
00:03:18,960 --> 00:03:21,000
She leaves it outside to be safe.

53
00:03:24,280 --> 00:03:25,440
Sylvia?

54
00:03:29,880 --> 00:03:31,560
Her clothes are gone!

55
00:03:35,320 --> 00:03:38,560
She had me worried sick.

56
00:03:38,680 --> 00:03:41,760
Her passport is gone. She's on the run.

57
00:03:41,920 --> 00:03:43,200
On the run? Why?

58
00:03:43,360 --> 00:03:45,920
You don't know why I needed to
find her so urgently?

59
00:03:46,080 --> 00:03:49,600
She borrowed $1M from a finance company
and I'm her guarantor.

60
00:03:49,680 --> 00:03:51,760
They're after me because
they can't find her.

61
00:03:51,840 --> 00:03:53,760
Wait...she owed $1M?

62
00:03:54,080 --> 00:03:55,400
I thought she had money to spare.

63
00:03:55,480 --> 00:03:56,680
She wanted me to invest with her.

64
00:03:56,800 --> 00:03:59,200
My daughter likes to make quick money.

65
00:03:59,360 --> 00:04:02,560
Last time she borrowed money for
margin trading.

66
00:04:02,680 --> 00:04:05,360
This is the second time she's on the run.

67
00:04:05,480 --> 00:04:07,200
Are you serious?

68
00:04:07,280 --> 00:04:09,880
You said she's been harassing you.

69
00:04:10,000 --> 00:04:12,200
That means she's in Hong Kong.

70
00:04:12,360 --> 00:04:14,000
I'll wait for her right here

71
00:04:14,080 --> 00:04:16,080
and see if she'll come back for her things.

72
00:04:16,200 --> 00:04:21,200
OK! Uncle, call me if you hear from her.

73
00:04:21,360 --> 00:04:22,640
OK...

74
00:04:23,320 --> 00:04:25,920
What are all those contraptions for?

75
00:04:26,080 --> 00:04:28,040
Is she after you?

76
00:05:04,200 --> 00:05:06,480
Did I just see a ghost?

77
00:05:06,560 --> 00:05:08,080
Or was I dreaming?

78
00:05:08,640 --> 00:05:11,040
Why was the TV turned off?

79
00:05:19,040 --> 00:05:21,440
Hello, Angie? Are you still up?

80
00:05:21,600 --> 00:05:26,960
I just woke up from a nightmare.

81
00:05:27,080 --> 00:05:28,960
And you? How's your end?

82
00:05:29,080 --> 00:05:30,240
Did you find Sylvia?

83
00:05:30,400 --> 00:05:32,080
Nobody answered the door.

84
00:05:32,200 --> 00:05:34,960
Uncle found her spare key.

85
00:05:35,080 --> 00:05:37,040
We got in and Sylvia left with her things.

86
00:05:37,120 --> 00:05:38,720
She also took her passport.

87
00:05:38,840 --> 00:05:40,320
She should be on the run.

88
00:05:40,480 --> 00:05:41,760
On the run?

89
00:05:41,840 --> 00:05:44,160
Yes, she's heavily in debt

90
00:05:44,280 --> 00:05:45,840
and the creditor chased Uncle.

91
00:05:45,960 --> 00:05:50,080
No wonder she was anxious for you
to invest with her.

92
00:05:50,200 --> 00:05:53,080
Maybe she needed the money.

93
00:05:53,200 --> 00:05:56,520
That's why when I told her I have
second thoughts about buying overseas,

94
00:05:56,640 --> 00:05:59,080
she threw a fit and forced me
to sell our flat.

95
00:05:59,200 --> 00:06:02,080
Did you discuss how to go forward?

96
00:06:02,200 --> 00:06:04,480
Uncle thinks she's running
from her creditors

97
00:06:04,640 --> 00:06:05,680
He's staying behind

98
00:06:05,840 --> 00:06:07,920
in case Sylvia comes back.

99
00:06:08,080 --> 00:06:10,800
I hope she can sort out her situation

100
00:06:10,920 --> 00:06:12,480
and leave us alone.

101
00:06:12,640 --> 00:06:14,800
Sylvia is unpredictable

102
00:06:14,920 --> 00:06:15,960
and often acts on an impulse.

103
00:06:16,080 --> 00:06:18,400
Be careful when you go out.

104
00:06:18,520 --> 00:06:21,760
OK. You should go to bed. Good night.

105
00:06:21,920 --> 00:06:22,960
Bye.

106
00:06:30,600 --> 00:06:33,680
Oh dear!

107
00:06:34,920 --> 00:06:37,600
Mom, you have anti-allergy meds?

108
00:06:38,600 --> 00:06:40,880
In the cabinet, get it yourself.

109
00:06:40,960 --> 00:06:43,280
We have both topical and oral meds.

110
00:06:47,840 --> 00:06:50,720
What happened to your orchids?

111
00:06:50,800 --> 00:06:53,960
That's what I want to know.

112
00:06:54,080 --> 00:06:57,040
Even if they were to wither,

113
00:06:57,200 --> 00:07:00,200
it should happen slowly and not overnight.

114
00:07:00,960 --> 00:07:02,400
Give me a hair.

115
00:07:02,520 --> 00:07:04,320
To perform black magic?

116
00:07:06,040 --> 00:07:08,160
Did she use black magic on me?

117
00:07:11,920 --> 00:07:13,840
Must find an excuse to lure her out.

118
00:07:14,920 --> 00:07:17,440
Sylvia, I have decided to go ahead
with the investment.

119
00:07:17,640 --> 00:07:20,320
Call me back. Let's talk about this.

120
00:07:29,520 --> 00:07:31,280
You're finally calling me back.

121
00:07:31,400 --> 00:07:34,400
I want to know if you truly want to
be with me,

122
00:07:34,520 --> 00:07:37,760
or you're just worried I'll go after
your beloved Angie

123
00:07:37,920 --> 00:07:39,200
and want to lure me out.

124
00:07:39,320 --> 00:07:41,040
I'm genuinely worried about you.

125
00:07:41,520 --> 00:07:44,320
Your Dad too. He came looking for you

126
00:07:44,400 --> 00:07:45,760
and is now waiting in your studio.

127
00:07:45,920 --> 00:07:48,000
He said you're in debt.

128
00:07:48,400 --> 00:07:50,320
Why can't he mind his own business?

129
00:07:50,480 --> 00:07:53,200
I know you reacted like this
because of money.

130
00:07:53,360 --> 00:07:55,600
Why don't I borrow money for you?

131
00:07:55,800 --> 00:07:56,880
Please stop doing this.

132
00:07:56,960 --> 00:07:59,040
Don't harass or hurt Angie anymore, OK?

133
00:07:59,160 --> 00:08:01,840
You think I'm with you because of money?

134
00:08:01,960 --> 00:08:06,400
You're willing to lend me money
all because of Angie.

135
00:08:06,520 --> 00:08:08,720
No. I genuinely want to help you.

136
00:08:09,400 --> 00:08:11,520
Let's meet and talk.

137
00:08:11,640 --> 00:08:13,960
It's better to put two minds together.

138
00:08:14,080 --> 00:08:14,880
Don't bother.

139
00:08:15,040 --> 00:08:18,480
You'll just discuss it with your ex again.

140
00:08:18,600 --> 00:08:20,800
You know what really pissed me off?

141
00:08:20,920 --> 00:08:24,000
It's not the money. But because
you lied to me.

142
00:08:24,160 --> 00:08:26,880
Sylvia, you got this all wrong.

143
00:08:27,000 --> 00:08:28,640
You love her that much?

144
00:08:28,800 --> 00:08:32,040
OK. Get ready to be star-crossed lovers.

145
00:08:32,160 --> 00:08:33,920
Hello? Sylvia...

146
00:08:39,320 --> 00:08:41,600
Mom, knock before you come in!

147
00:08:41,680 --> 00:08:43,600
What about my privacy?

148
00:08:43,760 --> 00:08:46,680
No matter, you're my son.

149
00:08:46,800 --> 00:08:49,600
Let's not get into that.

150
00:08:49,760 --> 00:08:50,720
I want to ask you,

151
00:08:50,880 --> 00:08:54,160
is Sylvia harassing you and Angie?

152
00:08:54,320 --> 00:08:55,760
You were eavesdropping?

153
00:08:55,920 --> 00:08:58,080
Would you tell me if I didn't?

154
00:08:58,240 --> 00:09:01,800
I knew that witch is bad news.

155
00:09:02,000 --> 00:09:03,520
I was right all along.

156
00:09:03,680 --> 00:09:06,480
You can't blame her. It was my fault.

157
00:09:06,640 --> 00:09:10,800
Don't feel guilty. She set you up, son.

158
00:09:10,920 --> 00:09:12,800
The day you fell off the hillside,

159
00:09:12,920 --> 00:09:14,320
I visited you at the hospital.

160
00:09:14,480 --> 00:09:16,400
Naturally, I looked in on Angie as well.

161
00:09:16,560 --> 00:09:20,080
I found out it was Angie
who saved your life.

162
00:09:21,120 --> 00:09:22,240
(five months before)

163
00:09:22,320 --> 00:09:24,240
You're in worse shape than Davis!?

164
00:09:24,400 --> 00:09:26,560
Don't worry, Auntie. I'm fine.

165
00:09:26,680 --> 00:09:29,600
Back then, Davis passed out

166
00:09:29,760 --> 00:09:32,400
and it was dangerous on the slope.

167
00:09:32,560 --> 00:09:35,440
I wanted to go get help,

168
00:09:35,560 --> 00:09:38,400
but I was worried to leave
Davis by himself out there.

169
00:09:38,520 --> 00:09:41,600
I pulled him up to somewhere flat.

170
00:09:41,760 --> 00:09:46,400
But I was a klutz and fell back down...

171
00:09:46,520 --> 00:09:49,280
So you saved Davis?

172
00:09:49,400 --> 00:09:50,880
Were you strong enough?

173
00:09:51,080 --> 00:09:55,600
Auntie, remember you drew a lot for us?

174
00:09:55,720 --> 00:09:57,440
I was thinking...

175
00:09:57,560 --> 00:10:00,400
if we stick with each other
and won't give up,

176
00:10:00,560 --> 00:10:02,880
we can overcome anything.

177
00:10:03,040 --> 00:10:06,400
Then I suddenly felt full of energy...

178
00:10:06,520 --> 00:10:07,600
That's amazing.

179
00:10:09,880 --> 00:10:11,360
How could you laugh about it?

180
00:10:11,440 --> 00:10:14,400
Why didn't you tell Davis you saved him

181
00:10:14,560 --> 00:10:17,680
and let him think the witch did?

182
00:10:17,800 --> 00:10:21,520
It doesn't matter.

183
00:10:21,600 --> 00:10:24,920
I didn't do it to make him feel grateful.

184
00:10:25,080 --> 00:10:28,920
Besides, he seems to hit it off with Sylvia.

185
00:10:29,080 --> 00:10:32,080
They're so sweet and he's so in love.

186
00:10:32,200 --> 00:10:35,040
It doesn't matter if I tell him or not.

187
00:10:35,720 --> 00:10:40,880
Your ex risked her life to save yours.

188
00:10:41,000 --> 00:10:44,160
But this witch is hurting you.

189
00:10:44,320 --> 00:10:46,880
See? Your skin is sensitive

190
00:10:47,040 --> 00:10:48,560
and you hurt your hands.

191
00:10:48,680 --> 00:10:51,760
I think she's definitely behind it.

192
00:10:51,880 --> 00:10:55,200
I don't know how you can get away.

193
00:10:55,480 --> 00:11:00,880
I better ask Uncle Kim what we can do.

194
00:11:17,160 --> 00:11:18,320
Angie!

195
00:11:19,920 --> 00:11:22,000
Get in. I'll take you to work.

196
00:11:23,040 --> 00:11:24,640
Why all of a sudden?

197
00:11:24,760 --> 00:11:26,880
You leave at 9:30 a.m.?

198
00:11:27,000 --> 00:11:28,480
Yes. Why?

199
00:11:28,600 --> 00:11:30,720
I'm worried Sylvia will
come after you again.

200
00:11:30,800 --> 00:11:34,800
I figure I'll take you to and from work, OK?

201
00:11:35,000 --> 00:11:37,520
OK. But won't that impose on you?

202
00:11:37,680 --> 00:11:40,560
I took time off. I spoke to the Boss.

203
00:11:40,720 --> 00:11:42,560
I didn't want my personal life to
affect my work.

204
00:11:42,720 --> 00:11:44,640
He told me to take two weeks off.

205
00:11:44,800 --> 00:11:45,920
I need to clear my annual leave anyway.

206
00:11:46,040 --> 00:11:49,040
You're going to stick with me 24 x 7?

207
00:11:49,160 --> 00:11:51,040
I'm not going back to the office today.

208
00:11:51,200 --> 00:11:52,080
Where are you going?

209
00:11:52,200 --> 00:11:55,120
I'm doing research in a walled village.

210
00:11:55,280 --> 00:11:57,600
I don't want you to be alone.

211
00:11:57,720 --> 00:12:00,000
Get in. I'll drop you.

212
00:12:04,280 --> 00:12:07,680
Sylvia finally called me back.

213
00:12:07,800 --> 00:12:10,640
I told her I'll borrow money for her

214
00:12:10,800 --> 00:12:12,560
but she bit my head off.

215
00:12:12,680 --> 00:12:16,640
She still thinks we got back together
behind her back.

216
00:12:16,760 --> 00:12:19,840
There's nothing we can do
if she doesn't believe you.

217
00:12:20,000 --> 00:12:23,520
Looks like she's still emotionally unstable.

218
00:12:23,680 --> 00:12:24,920
Has she been harassing you?

219
00:12:25,080 --> 00:12:29,040
No. But you can't pick me up every day

220
00:12:29,120 --> 00:12:30,920
and stick with me.

221
00:12:31,080 --> 00:12:32,560
We'll play by ear.

222
00:12:32,720 --> 00:12:35,360
At least try to reduce your chance
of being alone.

223
00:12:36,000 --> 00:12:38,880
But if she can harass us through the air,

224
00:12:39,000 --> 00:12:41,600
we must find a way to defend ourselves.

225
00:12:42,920 --> 00:12:45,680
There's still another way.

226
00:12:45,800 --> 00:12:46,880
Such as?

227
00:12:47,040 --> 00:12:49,600
I plan to leave Hong Kong.

228
00:12:49,720 --> 00:12:51,600
Are you running from Sylvia?

229
00:12:51,720 --> 00:12:55,120
She's behaving like this because
she got the wrong idea about us.

230
00:12:55,280 --> 00:12:58,160
If I leave, she'll get over it

231
00:12:58,320 --> 00:12:59,360
and she'll leave you alone.

232
00:12:59,520 --> 00:13:00,880
Of course not!

233
00:13:01,000 --> 00:13:03,280
There's no reason you should suffer
the consequences.

234
00:13:03,400 --> 00:13:06,080
You said you like Hong Kong.

235
00:13:06,240 --> 00:13:08,320
You shouldn't have to leave.

236
00:13:08,440 --> 00:13:11,360
OK...it was just an idea.

237
00:13:11,520 --> 00:13:13,520
I'm working on a new program,

238
00:13:13,680 --> 00:13:14,960
I can't leave yet.

239
00:13:15,120 --> 00:13:17,840
I'll think about it later.

240
00:13:25,600 --> 00:13:26,880
Here we are.

241
00:13:30,120 --> 00:13:31,680
This new program I'm doing

242
00:13:31,800 --> 00:13:34,560
is about the history and culture
of a walled village.

243
00:13:34,640 --> 00:13:35,920
I'm meeting the person in charge out here.

244
00:13:36,000 --> 00:13:37,120
She'll show me around.

245
00:13:37,200 --> 00:13:38,800
I should go. Thank you.

246
00:13:39,320 --> 00:13:41,200
I'll go with you.

247
00:13:42,440 --> 00:13:43,440
OK!

248
00:13:48,040 --> 00:13:52,560
Mom told me last time we fell down the slope

249
00:13:52,640 --> 00:13:54,640
it was you who pulled me back up.

250
00:13:54,760 --> 00:13:57,040
But all along, I thought it was Sylvia.

251
00:13:58,040 --> 00:14:01,680
It doesn't matter who actually saved you.

252
00:14:01,880 --> 00:14:03,200
What matters is you're fine.

253
00:14:03,280 --> 00:14:04,720
Of course not!

254
00:14:07,120 --> 00:14:09,680
Mom consulted a fortune teller,

255
00:14:09,840 --> 00:14:13,680
whoever goes through thick and thin
with me is my true love.

256
00:14:15,600 --> 00:14:19,360
If that's the case, when I was injured,

257
00:14:19,480 --> 00:14:23,280
the real person who saved me is crucial.

258
00:14:27,520 --> 00:14:29,840
Are you Miss Man?

259
00:14:39,280 --> 00:14:44,240
Auntie Mui, we're working on a program
called Historical Places.

260
00:14:44,320 --> 00:14:48,320
It features the local customs and
history of this place.

261
00:14:48,400 --> 00:14:50,480
You came to the right person.

262
00:14:50,600 --> 00:14:53,040
My family has been living here
for several generations.

263
00:14:53,160 --> 00:14:56,000
We help Mr. Chow look after the mansion.

264
00:14:56,360 --> 00:14:58,880
You can film inside,

265
00:14:59,000 --> 00:15:02,080
but make sure you don't lose anything.

266
00:15:02,240 --> 00:15:05,200
Or else Mr. Chow will scold me
when he returns from overseas.

267
00:15:05,320 --> 00:15:06,720
Don't worry!

268
00:15:06,840 --> 00:15:08,880
We'll try not to touch anything.

269
00:15:09,040 --> 00:15:10,880
Good. Follow me.

270
00:15:10,960 --> 00:15:11,760
OK!

271
00:15:15,320 --> 00:15:18,000
This mansion has a long history

272
00:15:18,120 --> 00:15:20,080
that has passed through several generations.

273
00:15:20,200 --> 00:15:22,480
This is the courtyard.

274
00:15:23,760 --> 00:15:26,400
My mother was a servant.

275
00:15:26,560 --> 00:15:28,400
When I was little,

276
00:15:28,560 --> 00:15:32,160
I loved listening to her telling
stories of this place,

277
00:15:32,280 --> 00:15:34,560
especially about Mr. Chow.

278
00:15:34,680 --> 00:15:37,600
You said this place was passed down
for many generations,

279
00:15:37,760 --> 00:15:40,400
what period did Mr. Chow live in?

280
00:15:40,520 --> 00:15:45,600
Probably 100 years ago.

281
00:15:45,680 --> 00:15:48,240
During the early days of the Republic?

282
00:15:48,320 --> 00:15:49,200
Yes.

283
00:15:49,360 --> 00:15:51,280
I'll show you the master bedroom.

284
00:15:51,360 --> 00:15:52,160
Great.

285
00:15:58,000 --> 00:16:03,120
Mother told me Mr. Chow lived here
after he got married.

286
00:16:03,320 --> 00:16:05,920
But only for a short time.

287
00:16:06,040 --> 00:16:07,920
Nobody has lived here ever since.

288
00:16:23,160 --> 00:16:25,680
What? You have seen the wedding gown before?

289
00:16:27,880 --> 00:16:29,200
I think so.

290
00:16:29,360 --> 00:16:31,760
Auntie Mui, why did the owner,
I mean Mr. Chow

291
00:16:31,880 --> 00:16:33,680
leave the wedding gown here?

292
00:16:33,880 --> 00:16:35,920
I told you last time you were here.

293
00:16:36,040 --> 00:16:38,160
Nobody left it hanging.

294
00:16:38,320 --> 00:16:40,640
I wasn't here last time.

295
00:16:40,800 --> 00:16:42,480
Don't deny it.

296
00:16:42,640 --> 00:16:44,840
If you're forgetful, do what Ms. Man did,

297
00:16:44,960 --> 00:16:47,400
jot it down in a notebook.

298
00:16:48,440 --> 00:16:50,120
Right...I'm forgetful.

299
00:16:50,240 --> 00:16:52,000
Can you tell me again?

300
00:16:52,160 --> 00:16:53,080
OK.

301
00:16:53,200 --> 00:16:56,000
Mother said the wedding gown

302
00:16:56,120 --> 00:16:58,200
belonged to one of the servants.

303
00:16:58,360 --> 00:17:00,400
She was getting married

304
00:17:00,520 --> 00:17:02,600
but the groom broke off the engagement

305
00:17:02,760 --> 00:17:05,680
and she died wearing the wedding gown.

306
00:17:06,320 --> 00:17:08,600
Why leave this ominous gown hanging there?

307
00:17:08,720 --> 00:17:12,960
That's just it...everyone saw the girl
buried in the gown.

308
00:17:13,160 --> 00:17:16,600
On the seventh day after the girl died,

309
00:17:16,720 --> 00:17:19,520
people in the mansion saw the gown
hanging in this room.

310
00:17:19,680 --> 00:17:22,360
Later on, whoever tried to take
the gown away,

311
00:17:22,480 --> 00:17:25,440
something bad would happen.

312
00:17:25,560 --> 00:17:29,320
They either tripped and fell, hurt
their hands or bumped their heads.

313
00:17:29,400 --> 00:17:31,360
In the end, no one dared touch it again

314
00:17:31,520 --> 00:17:32,840
and just left it hanging there.

315
00:17:32,960 --> 00:17:34,720
That's spooky.

316
00:17:34,840 --> 00:17:36,480
Of course it is!

317
00:17:36,640 --> 00:17:39,600
The girl was mean and nasty.

318
00:17:39,720 --> 00:17:42,000
When she found out her fiance dumper her,

319
00:17:42,120 --> 00:17:44,400
she picked up an axe

320
00:17:44,520 --> 00:17:47,440
and hacked the tree under which
they pledged their love.

321
00:17:47,560 --> 00:17:50,960
She almost chopped it down.

322
00:17:55,400 --> 00:17:56,720
Bye!
Bye!

323
00:18:00,440 --> 00:18:03,360
When Auntie Mui was telling us the story
about that girl,

324
00:18:03,440 --> 00:18:05,920
you were entranced. What were you thinking?

325
00:18:06,080 --> 00:18:09,320
Nothing. Sylvia's Dad contacted me

326
00:18:09,440 --> 00:18:12,160
and told me more about her past.

327
00:18:12,320 --> 00:18:13,120
What did he say?

328
00:18:13,280 --> 00:18:15,920
She's rather self-centered and moody.

329
00:18:16,040 --> 00:18:17,360
Anything goes when she likes something,

330
00:18:17,480 --> 00:18:19,760
but when she doesn't like it,
she'll go crazy.

331
00:18:20,360 --> 00:18:22,720
No wonder she tried to come between us.

332
00:18:22,880 --> 00:18:26,720
There's more...he said one time
her boyfriend wanted to break up with her,

333
00:18:26,840 --> 00:18:28,720
she was so pissed she showed up
at his house...

334
00:18:28,840 --> 00:18:29,680
Hey!

335
00:18:29,760 --> 00:18:31,440
Come on, Honey!

336
00:18:31,560 --> 00:18:32,800
The guy is not right for you.

337
00:18:32,920 --> 00:18:34,160
Forget him. Find someone else.

338
00:18:34,320 --> 00:18:35,640
Forget him?
Come on...

339
00:18:35,760 --> 00:18:37,880
I won't let it slide.
Honey...

340
00:18:38,000 --> 00:18:39,640
Out of my way!
Let's go...

341
00:18:39,720 --> 00:18:42,000
You come any closer, I'll hack you too.

342
00:18:50,480 --> 00:18:52,600
That's why when Auntie Mui said

343
00:18:52,680 --> 00:18:54,560
after the girl's fiance broke off
the engagement,

344
00:18:54,640 --> 00:18:55,640
she hacked the tree,

345
00:18:55,720 --> 00:18:58,120
I remember when Sylvia's boyfriend
cheated on her,

346
00:18:58,200 --> 00:18:59,440
she hacked his door.

347
00:18:59,520 --> 00:19:01,840
They both hacked something with an axe.

348
00:19:03,280 --> 00:19:04,880
Am I making it sound too scary?

349
00:19:04,960 --> 00:19:06,480
Maybe I'm overthinking.

350
00:19:06,680 --> 00:19:08,480
Remember I told you

351
00:19:08,600 --> 00:19:11,080
since Sylvia started harassing us,

352
00:19:11,200 --> 00:19:13,680
I often had nightmares?

353
00:19:13,880 --> 00:19:18,280
Once, a girl wearing a Chinese wedding gown

354
00:19:18,400 --> 00:19:20,720
flashed in front of my eyes.

355
00:19:20,840 --> 00:19:23,040
I couldn't decide if I was dreaming,

356
00:19:23,200 --> 00:19:24,880
or it was real.

357
00:19:25,080 --> 00:19:29,120
But I remember the wedding gown
she was wearing,

358
00:19:29,240 --> 00:19:33,640
was very similar to the one hanging in
Mr. Chow's room.

359
00:19:33,760 --> 00:19:35,560
What a coincidence!

360
00:19:35,720 --> 00:19:38,320
Sylvia and that girl had things in common.

361
00:19:38,480 --> 00:19:40,360
You were doing this new program

362
00:19:40,520 --> 00:19:42,600
and stumbled up the wedding gown.

363
00:19:42,760 --> 00:19:46,160
Somehow, things are connected.

364
00:19:47,080 --> 00:19:51,560
Is Sylvia somehow connected to this place?

365
00:19:54,000 --> 00:19:55,840
We better believe it.

366
00:19:55,960 --> 00:19:59,880
Like Mom said, we may need the help
of a professional.

367
00:20:03,920 --> 00:20:07,840
Uncle Kim, this is more than bad luck
in romance.

368
00:20:08,000 --> 00:20:10,400
How can we resolve this?

369
00:20:10,560 --> 00:20:14,480
Don't worry, let me try to understand
this better.

370
00:20:14,640 --> 00:20:17,880
You just said Sylvia's behavior

371
00:20:18,000 --> 00:20:20,960
was very similar to that girl
from the mansion.

372
00:20:21,120 --> 00:20:25,280
Other than using an axe,
what else is very similar?

373
00:20:25,400 --> 00:20:27,080
Maybe not.

374
00:20:27,640 --> 00:20:29,680
I asked Sylvia's Dad,

375
00:20:29,760 --> 00:20:31,560
he can't seem to put his finger on

376
00:20:31,680 --> 00:20:33,080
how Sylvia was connected to
the walled village.

377
00:20:33,240 --> 00:20:37,200
That's why we think it may be
just a coincidence.

378
00:20:37,360 --> 00:20:40,040
Nothing in this world is a coincidence.

379
00:20:40,160 --> 00:20:41,840
We call it a coincidence because

380
00:20:41,960 --> 00:20:45,120
we have yet to uncover the profundity
or its cause and effect.

381
00:20:45,240 --> 00:20:51,440
Remember how you first came across
the mansion in the walled village?

382
00:20:51,560 --> 00:20:56,280
A friend of mine dragged me to
pray to the Lover's Rock.

383
00:20:56,400 --> 00:20:59,720
After that, we threw a wishing placard
onto the wishing tree.

384
00:20:59,800 --> 00:21:01,200
Are you ready to go?

385
00:21:12,960 --> 00:21:15,200
Don't run after it. Throw another one.

386
00:21:25,320 --> 00:21:29,200
I had a feeling when I saw the mansion.

387
00:21:29,280 --> 00:21:33,040
I was thinking about doing a program
like Historical Places.

388
00:21:33,160 --> 00:21:35,360
I wanted to see if it's doable.

389
00:21:35,520 --> 00:21:38,840
So I asked the caretaker, Auntie Mui

390
00:21:38,960 --> 00:21:41,680
to let me take a peek inside.

391
00:21:43,400 --> 00:21:48,520
She told me Mr. Chow, the owner of
the mansion is very rich.

392
00:21:49,760 --> 00:21:53,040
I walked past Mr. Chow's bedroom

393
00:21:53,160 --> 00:21:54,720
but I didn't go inside,

394
00:21:54,880 --> 00:21:57,640
and didn't notice the wedding gown.

395
00:21:57,800 --> 00:22:00,240
Until we decided to do the show,

396
00:22:00,360 --> 00:22:02,120
I interviewed Auntie Mui again

397
00:22:02,240 --> 00:22:04,040
and I recognized the wedding gown.

398
00:22:04,120 --> 00:22:10,720
It was the same as the one I saw
in my dream or in an illusion.

399
00:22:21,960 --> 00:22:25,640
At first, I thought since this mansion
has such a long history,

400
00:22:25,760 --> 00:22:27,680
there should be plenty of stories to tell.

401
00:22:27,760 --> 00:22:29,440
That's why I took on this project.

402
00:22:29,560 --> 00:22:32,120
But it never dawned on me

403
00:22:32,200 --> 00:22:34,880
the story behind is much more
complicated than I thought.

404
00:22:34,960 --> 00:22:39,640
The gown you saw...whether in a dream
or an illusion

405
00:22:39,720 --> 00:22:41,000
was exactly the same?

406
00:22:41,080 --> 00:22:43,160
Or just a similar style?

407
00:22:43,240 --> 00:22:44,560
No.

408
00:22:44,680 --> 00:22:47,360
The embroidery was very special.

409
00:22:47,440 --> 00:22:50,120
That's why I'm sure it was the same one.

410
00:22:51,160 --> 00:22:55,040
That's really scary and bizarre.

411
00:22:55,120 --> 00:22:58,640
When the maid and Sylvia were dumped,

412
00:22:58,720 --> 00:23:00,360
they both hacked something with an axe.

413
00:23:00,480 --> 00:23:02,320
After Sylvia harassed you,

414
00:23:02,400 --> 00:23:04,320
you saw the wedding gown.

415
00:23:04,400 --> 00:23:06,640
When the dog led you to the mansion,

416
00:23:06,720 --> 00:23:09,800
you saw the gown in Mr. Chow's room.

417
00:23:10,000 --> 00:23:12,640
The course of nature went around

418
00:23:12,760 --> 00:23:15,640
and determined the chance of
you three meeting each other.

419
00:23:15,760 --> 00:23:19,120
The chance of Angie seeing the gown

420
00:23:19,200 --> 00:23:22,560
and finding the mansion

421
00:23:22,640 --> 00:23:26,120
proved you have an indissoluble bond
with this place.

422
00:23:26,280 --> 00:23:28,600
The grudge Sylvia holds against you

423
00:23:28,720 --> 00:23:30,960
should be more than out of jealousy.

424
00:23:31,120 --> 00:23:34,160
That witch is vicious, it's definitely
bad karma.

425
00:23:34,320 --> 00:23:36,360
How can we resolve this?

426
00:23:36,480 --> 00:23:38,240
You can't.

427
00:23:38,400 --> 00:23:39,360
No way to resolve it?

428
00:23:39,520 --> 00:23:42,160
Uncle Kim, you told me in the past,

429
00:23:42,360 --> 00:23:45,120
anything can be resolved.

430
00:23:45,240 --> 00:23:47,200
He's my only child,

431
00:23:47,360 --> 00:23:49,520
you must think of a way to help him.

432
00:23:49,680 --> 00:23:51,440
Unless you avoid her completely

433
00:23:51,600 --> 00:23:53,360
and go as far away as possible.

434
00:23:53,480 --> 00:23:56,720
Actually I have considered
emigrating overseas.

435
00:23:57,520 --> 00:23:59,600
Don't be reckless.

436
00:23:59,720 --> 00:24:01,640
This is just our wild guess.

437
00:24:01,760 --> 00:24:05,200
If you want to find out more,

438
00:24:05,320 --> 00:24:07,920
I know someone who can help you.

439
00:24:13,760 --> 00:24:15,440
Is hypnosis difficult?

440
00:24:15,520 --> 00:24:18,400
Usually, you only need to relax.

441
00:24:18,560 --> 00:24:20,120
Are you ready?

442
00:24:22,240 --> 00:24:24,800
OK, close your eyes.

443
00:24:25,800 --> 00:24:27,640
Take a deep breath.

444
00:24:27,760 --> 00:24:30,400
Try your best to relax

445
00:24:30,560 --> 00:24:32,880
and release all your pressure.

446
00:24:33,320 --> 00:24:35,320
Slowly raise your right hand.

447
00:24:36,280 --> 00:24:38,720
Imagine you're holding a bucket

448
00:24:38,880 --> 00:24:41,760
and water is slowly filling up the bucket.

449
00:24:41,880 --> 00:24:45,920
As the water is filling up,

450
00:24:46,000 --> 00:24:47,920
the bucket becomes heavy.

451
00:24:48,040 --> 00:24:49,760
Then I would count from one to three.

452
00:24:49,880 --> 00:24:51,440
On my count to three,

453
00:24:51,600 --> 00:24:54,960
let your subconscious go as far as possible.

454
00:24:55,600 --> 00:24:59,360
1...2...3...

455
00:25:03,400 --> 00:25:04,840
(Chow's Mansion)

456
00:25:17,000 --> 00:25:18,840
Where's Ning-yuk's bridal sedan chair?

457
00:25:18,920 --> 00:25:21,080
Master, it's not yet the auspicious hour.

458
00:25:21,120 --> 00:25:22,520
Be patient.

459
00:25:55,360 --> 00:25:57,080
Why did we stop?

460
00:25:57,160 --> 00:25:59,360
A jinx is in the way.

461
00:25:59,480 --> 00:26:02,400
Don't talk nonsense! Who is it?

462
00:26:02,520 --> 00:26:05,200
Master Chow has a child bride
called On-yee.

463
00:26:05,360 --> 00:26:08,160
She's getting married on the same day.

464
00:26:08,320 --> 00:26:11,120
I don't think so. She did this on purpose.

465
00:26:11,240 --> 00:26:13,400
The child bride was sold to the Chow family

466
00:26:13,480 --> 00:26:15,920
when she was little.

467
00:26:16,040 --> 00:26:19,440
She thought she'd marry the young master
when she grew up.

468
00:26:19,560 --> 00:26:21,920
But you're marrying the young master,

469
00:26:22,040 --> 00:26:24,880
and the young master also found her
a suitable husband.

470
00:26:25,040 --> 00:26:27,800
But this child bride held a grudge

471
00:26:27,920 --> 00:26:29,680
and wanted revenge.

472
00:26:29,800 --> 00:26:31,800
What do you mean, Master Sin?

473
00:26:31,920 --> 00:26:34,720
It's a taboo for a wedding to clash
with another wedding.

474
00:26:34,840 --> 00:26:37,360
Now we have two brides getting married
on the same day

475
00:26:37,520 --> 00:26:40,480
and the bridal sedan chairs clashed.

476
00:26:40,600 --> 00:26:43,440
When two happy occasions clashed,

477
00:26:43,600 --> 00:26:45,120
it will bring bad luck.

478
00:26:45,280 --> 00:26:48,120
At best, the marriage will break up.

479
00:26:48,240 --> 00:26:51,080
Worse yet, there will be bloodshed.

480
00:26:51,200 --> 00:26:53,320
If Master Sin says so,

481
00:26:53,440 --> 00:26:56,360
Ling-yee, we should let them through.

482
00:26:56,520 --> 00:26:57,360
OK.

483
00:26:57,440 --> 00:27:00,400
Porter, let's go around.

484
00:27:29,320 --> 00:27:30,760
Early years of the Republic?

485
00:27:30,880 --> 00:27:32,560
That was over 100 years ago.

486
00:27:32,680 --> 00:27:34,280
You recognize any of those people?

487
00:27:34,400 --> 00:27:36,600
I don't recognize any of them.

488
00:27:36,720 --> 00:27:41,760
But Master Chow and his bride

489
00:27:41,880 --> 00:27:44,760
gave me a feeling of deja vu.

490
00:27:44,880 --> 00:27:46,400
If that's the case,

491
00:27:46,600 --> 00:27:48,880
the servant Auntie Mui mentioned

492
00:27:49,040 --> 00:27:52,120
should be the child bride.

493
00:27:52,240 --> 00:27:54,520
She's too barbaric.

494
00:27:55,480 --> 00:27:57,920
How can we resolve the situation?

495
00:27:58,080 --> 00:28:00,160
How can we do that?

496
00:28:03,400 --> 00:28:05,880
Davis, what are you thinking?

497
00:28:07,360 --> 00:28:08,720
I'm thinking...

498
00:28:09,360 --> 00:28:12,560
if I could piece back
together the whole story

499
00:28:12,640 --> 00:28:17,120
and find out more about our
connections with Master Chow...

500
00:28:17,280 --> 00:28:19,040
Too bad I was too nervous.

501
00:28:19,160 --> 00:28:21,360
The hypnotist said I wasn't relaxed enough

502
00:28:21,480 --> 00:28:23,840
and couldn't get into a hypnotic state.

503
00:28:24,560 --> 00:28:27,680
Davis, you just said if
you were Master Chow...

504
00:28:27,840 --> 00:28:30,840
Does that mean there's a chance you're not?

505
00:28:31,000 --> 00:28:32,760
I don't know.

506
00:28:32,960 --> 00:28:35,920
Maybe because we didn't see it
with our own eyes,

507
00:28:36,000 --> 00:28:37,920
that's why just like you,

508
00:28:38,040 --> 00:28:40,400
we have the feeling of deja vu.

509
00:28:41,760 --> 00:28:44,880
There's actually another way.

510
00:28:45,000 --> 00:28:47,560
Now we know about Master Chow's mansion

511
00:28:47,680 --> 00:28:49,680
and the Chows have descendants.

512
00:28:49,800 --> 00:28:53,640
That means someone should know
what happened back then.

513
00:28:53,760 --> 00:28:56,720
Inside the walled village, we should
be able to find...

514
00:28:56,840 --> 00:28:59,360
information on Master Chow and Miss Koo.

515
00:28:59,480 --> 00:29:01,680
Let's go inside the walled village again.

516
00:29:01,800 --> 00:29:04,280
You're doing research with me?

517
00:29:04,360 --> 00:29:06,280
I made copies of the genealogy
of the Chow clan

518
00:29:06,360 --> 00:29:07,240
and some old photos.

519
00:29:07,320 --> 00:29:08,200
You can take these with you.

520
00:29:08,240 --> 00:29:09,480
Thank you, Chief.

521
00:29:09,560 --> 00:29:12,400
You're welcome. Let me know
when the show goes on air.

522
00:29:12,480 --> 00:29:13,320
No problem.

523
00:29:13,400 --> 00:29:14,160
I should get going.

524
00:29:14,240 --> 00:29:15,920
OK. Thank you.
Bye!

525
00:29:17,400 --> 00:29:19,360
It's definitely him.

526
00:29:19,840 --> 00:29:23,200
Master Chow looked exactly like him.

527
00:29:23,280 --> 00:29:25,280
And all these paintings?

528
00:29:25,400 --> 00:29:27,120
Master Chow drew them.

529
00:29:27,800 --> 00:29:30,840
The village Chief said his name was Kai-hin.

530
00:29:30,960 --> 00:29:33,520
That means these were all his paintings.

531
00:29:33,640 --> 00:29:35,640
But these are oil paintings.

532
00:29:35,760 --> 00:29:38,280
Maybe he studied overseas

533
00:29:38,400 --> 00:29:40,400
and learnt Western painting

534
00:29:40,520 --> 00:29:43,680
just like Xu Beihong and Wu Zuoren

535
00:29:43,800 --> 00:29:45,680
went to France to learn painting,

536
00:29:45,800 --> 00:29:48,120
sketching and oil painting.

537
00:29:48,800 --> 00:29:51,440
This is similar to your paintings.

538
00:29:56,720 --> 00:30:00,880
Look! I found Master Chow's diary.

539
00:30:01,080 --> 00:30:02,400
Thanks, Auntie Mui.

540
00:30:02,560 --> 00:30:04,360
Where have I seen you before?

541
00:30:05,600 --> 00:30:08,880
I'll leave you alone. Help yourselves.

542
00:30:09,000 --> 00:30:09,880
I'll go prepare dinner.

543
00:30:10,000 --> 00:30:11,640
OK. Thanks, Auntie Mui.

544
00:30:17,480 --> 00:30:19,280
It's more than a diary.

545
00:30:19,400 --> 00:30:21,120
There are recipes inside.

546
00:30:21,320 --> 00:30:23,040
But the handwriting is different.

547
00:30:23,160 --> 00:30:26,480
It looks like the handwriting of a woman.

548
00:30:26,600 --> 00:30:29,760
I remember Master Chow's wife's
last name is Koo.

549
00:30:29,920 --> 00:30:33,360
Koo Ning-yuk should have written
these recipes.

550
00:30:35,360 --> 00:30:39,120
I didn't realize Miss Koo
was a good cook like you.

551
00:30:39,240 --> 00:30:42,280
And like you, Master Chow liked to paint

552
00:30:42,400 --> 00:30:45,880
and preferred Western sketching
which was uncommon back then.

553
00:30:46,040 --> 00:30:49,640
And he loved drawing his wife
very much too.

554
00:31:05,280 --> 00:31:07,200
When I was hypnotized,

555
00:31:07,320 --> 00:31:09,080
I saw the wishing tree.

556
00:31:10,160 --> 00:31:13,280
It should be the one hacked by
the child bride.

557
00:31:25,600 --> 00:31:30,880
The marks are still here
after all these years.

558
00:31:31,440 --> 00:31:33,280
People didn't know what to do.

559
00:31:33,400 --> 00:31:36,720
The tree didn't heal.
That's why there are scars.

560
00:31:36,840 --> 00:31:39,680
Master Chow and Miss Koo owed her nothing.

561
00:31:39,800 --> 00:31:43,680
Maybe the child bride only behaved
in a fit of rage.

562
00:31:43,840 --> 00:31:48,600
Just think, Sylvia lied to you
from the start.

563
00:31:48,720 --> 00:31:51,280
When you discovered the lie
and you broke up with her,

564
00:31:51,440 --> 00:31:53,920
she began her revenge.

565
00:31:54,080 --> 00:31:59,520
Auntie Mui said the child bride
died in that wedding gown,

566
00:31:59,640 --> 00:32:03,120
which means she was full of
resentment and remorse...

567
00:32:03,320 --> 00:32:06,160
Angie, I know what you're worried about.

568
00:32:06,640 --> 00:32:09,680
She clashed the wedding
but she also died from it.

569
00:32:09,840 --> 00:32:11,760
Maybe that was her retribution.

570
00:32:11,880 --> 00:32:14,080
And it didn't affect Master Chow
and Miss Koo.

571
00:32:14,200 --> 00:32:15,440
But the question is

572
00:32:15,520 --> 00:32:19,440
we don't know what happened to
Master Chow and Miss Koo.

573
00:32:19,600 --> 00:32:22,840
No. I should leave Hong Kong ASAP.

574
00:32:22,960 --> 00:32:25,360
The sooner she gets over it,
she won't hurt you anymore.

575
00:32:25,480 --> 00:32:27,440
Angie...don't go.

576
00:32:28,760 --> 00:32:30,480
I don't want you to leave me.

577
00:32:33,480 --> 00:32:35,360
I don't care about Sylvia's background

578
00:32:35,520 --> 00:32:37,360
or what she'll do to us.

579
00:32:38,320 --> 00:32:41,280
I will stick with you and protect you.

580
00:32:49,320 --> 00:32:52,880
Angie, we should get back together.

581
00:32:56,200 --> 00:33:04,080
Davis, we acted on an impulse once.

582
00:33:05,360 --> 00:33:08,400
Besides, so much has happened lately.

583
00:33:09,680 --> 00:33:13,680
I think we should calm down first

584
00:33:15,520 --> 00:33:17,840
and think things over later, OK?

585
00:33:39,600 --> 00:33:40,400
Liz...

586
00:33:43,240 --> 00:33:44,480
How are you?

587
00:33:44,600 --> 00:33:47,200
Auntie said she's worried about you.

588
00:33:47,360 --> 00:33:50,320
You haven't eaten or gone out
in the past few days.

589
00:33:50,440 --> 00:33:51,720
Are you sick?

590
00:33:51,880 --> 00:33:54,480
Did you have a fight with Roy?

591
00:33:54,680 --> 00:33:56,240
Don't talk about him.

592
00:33:56,360 --> 00:33:57,600
How are you lately?

593
00:33:57,720 --> 00:34:01,920
I'm OK. Davis has been with me lately.

594
00:34:02,080 --> 00:34:04,400
You should stay away from him.

595
00:34:04,600 --> 00:34:06,680
He'll get you killed.

596
00:34:06,800 --> 00:34:08,760
Didn't you say you want to leave?

597
00:34:08,880 --> 00:34:10,760
Stop dragging your feet.

598
00:34:10,880 --> 00:34:13,640
He wants me to stay.

599
00:34:13,760 --> 00:34:16,720
Stay? Why?

600
00:34:16,840 --> 00:34:19,120
You want to get back together with him?

601
00:34:19,240 --> 00:34:21,240
That guy can't be trusted.

602
00:34:21,360 --> 00:34:23,920
What spell did he cast on you?

603
00:34:24,080 --> 00:34:26,160
You tried it once and it didn't work.

604
00:34:26,320 --> 00:34:27,840
He won't change.

605
00:34:27,960 --> 00:34:29,840
I think he has changed.

606
00:34:29,920 --> 00:34:31,920
He's more sincere compared to before.

607
00:34:32,040 --> 00:34:33,360
You're hopeless.

608
00:34:33,480 --> 00:34:35,440
You fell under his charm and
changed your tune.

609
00:34:35,640 --> 00:34:38,000
I have nothing to say to you. Just go.

610
00:34:50,760 --> 00:34:54,560
Liz...how unusual of you to ask me out.

611
00:34:55,360 --> 00:34:56,640
Only because of Angie.

612
00:34:56,720 --> 00:34:58,880
Or else, I don't want to see you.

613
00:34:59,080 --> 00:35:00,760
I urge you to let go.

614
00:35:02,120 --> 00:35:05,840
This is between Angie and me.

615
00:35:05,960 --> 00:35:07,880
You have the right to decide.

616
00:35:08,000 --> 00:35:09,640
Angie simply can't get over you.

617
00:35:09,760 --> 00:35:11,200
If she continues to stick with you,

618
00:35:11,280 --> 00:35:13,040
she'll just get hurt again.

619
00:35:13,160 --> 00:35:15,840
You and I both care about Angie.

620
00:35:15,960 --> 00:35:19,040
I can assure you, I won't hurt her again.

621
00:35:19,160 --> 00:35:20,880
I will protect her and take care of her.

622
00:35:20,960 --> 00:35:22,320
If you could do that,

623
00:35:22,400 --> 00:35:24,200
you wouldn't have gotten a divorce.

624
00:35:24,320 --> 00:35:26,840
You're a player, Angie is a homebody.

625
00:35:26,960 --> 00:35:30,400
I beg you to continue to be
your legless bird.

626
00:35:30,520 --> 00:35:32,760
Give Angie a chance to meet a decent man.

627
00:35:32,880 --> 00:35:34,800
Then we can all feel better.

628
00:35:37,400 --> 00:35:41,160
Do you know why there's an eraser
on a pencil?

629
00:35:44,080 --> 00:35:46,240
Because people make mistakes.

630
00:35:46,400 --> 00:35:50,200
Mistakes can be atoned.

631
00:35:51,960 --> 00:35:54,880
Give us another chance, OK?

632
00:36:03,160 --> 00:36:06,320
(There was a man)

633
00:36:09,160 --> 00:36:12,160
(That sailed the seas)

634
00:36:15,360 --> 00:36:18,760
(He left his woman)

635
00:36:21,800 --> 00:36:24,760
(behind to leave)

636
00:36:28,440 --> 00:36:32,000
(He kissed his children)

637
00:36:34,920 --> 00:36:37,680
(And turned to go)

638
00:36:41,160 --> 00:36:42,720
(And don't you cry)

639
00:36:42,840 --> 00:36:45,840
I told you the Observatory predicted
rain for today.

640
00:36:46,000 --> 00:36:48,240
Luckily, it didn't get wet.

641
00:36:48,400 --> 00:36:51,360
(I'm coming home)

642
00:36:54,000 --> 00:36:56,400
(There was a ship)

643
00:37:00,000 --> 00:37:03,600
(That sailed the seas)

644
00:37:04,320 --> 00:37:05,680
What are you painting?

645
00:37:05,760 --> 00:37:07,920
The leaves are not in full bloom.

646
00:37:08,600 --> 00:37:11,520
No, they look very pretty.

647
00:37:13,000 --> 00:37:16,160
Wow! That's pretty. When did you finish?

648
00:37:16,240 --> 00:37:19,640
I know I can't promise you anything.

649
00:37:19,800 --> 00:37:23,640
When you start something, it's best
to carry through the end.

650
00:37:25,920 --> 00:37:29,640
We don't know how this will end.

651
00:37:31,640 --> 00:37:34,480
I know you like things well-planned

652
00:37:34,600 --> 00:37:36,480
and you need a sense of security.

653
00:37:36,600 --> 00:37:39,040
Last time I wanted to paint
the leaves out here,

654
00:37:39,160 --> 00:37:43,280
you knew the Observatory predicted rain
and still came with me.

655
00:37:45,160 --> 00:37:48,240
But we didn't finish the painting.

656
00:37:49,360 --> 00:37:51,840
Who would have guessed before
we left home today,

657
00:37:51,920 --> 00:37:54,080
we actually checked the weather report.

658
00:37:54,200 --> 00:37:59,360
I guess we should finish the painting today.

659
00:38:02,640 --> 00:38:04,560
I'm quite sure

660
00:38:04,640 --> 00:38:07,440
I don't want this moment to be the end.

661
00:38:07,600 --> 00:38:10,640
Just like the lot Mom drew for us,

662
00:38:10,760 --> 00:38:14,160
if we stick together and don't give up,

663
00:38:14,280 --> 00:38:16,880
we can overcome anything.

664
00:38:21,840 --> 00:38:24,400
Angie, promise me,

665
00:38:26,120 --> 00:38:28,400
let's get back together?

666
00:38:29,240 --> 00:38:33,120
We can tackle any problem.

667
00:38:36,800 --> 00:38:39,760
(Don't you cry)

668
00:38:42,920 --> 00:38:47,520
(He's coming home)

669
00:38:52,800 --> 00:38:56,320
Sir, Siu Zi-yiu has been harassing us
for quite some time.

670
00:38:56,520 --> 00:38:58,640
My ex-wife and I have been wounded.

671
00:38:58,760 --> 00:39:01,840
I don't know how she did it.
She gave us rashes and bruises.

672
00:39:02,000 --> 00:39:04,000
We want to speak to her but
can't find her.

673
00:39:04,120 --> 00:39:05,440
Can you find her for us?

674
00:39:05,560 --> 00:39:07,960
Mr. Yau, we opened a file for you.

675
00:39:08,080 --> 00:39:10,560
We'll conduct an investigation based on
the information you provided.

676
00:39:10,720 --> 00:39:13,440
If you hear anything, please contact us.

677
00:39:14,240 --> 00:39:15,760
You've been investigating long enough.

678
00:39:15,840 --> 00:39:18,160
What have you found out?

679
00:39:18,280 --> 00:39:19,520
We're working on it.

680
00:39:19,640 --> 00:39:21,640
For you to come to the
Police station every day

681
00:39:21,760 --> 00:39:23,040
will only get in our way.

682
00:39:23,160 --> 00:39:24,560
I'm in your way?

683
00:39:24,680 --> 00:39:27,520
When will your investigation end?

684
00:39:27,640 --> 00:39:30,000
Don't worry. We'll call you
if we hear anything.

685
00:39:30,120 --> 00:39:31,680
Don't worry?

686
00:39:31,760 --> 00:39:34,400
Uncle...any word on Sylvia?

687
00:39:34,640 --> 00:39:35,440
Yes!

688
00:39:35,560 --> 00:39:36,840
Sylvia appeared in my dream.

689
00:39:36,920 --> 00:39:39,600
She said it was hot and stuffy where she is.

690
00:39:39,960 --> 00:39:42,160
I'm Kwan Zhi-fung of the Crime Unit
in New Territories East.

691
00:39:42,280 --> 00:39:43,840
Are you Mr. Siu Bong-chak?

692
00:39:43,920 --> 00:39:46,800
Sir, did something happen to my daughter?

693
00:39:46,920 --> 00:39:49,920
The MPU found her car in the mountains.

694
00:39:50,040 --> 00:39:53,040
The Police found the last image
of Sylvia's car

695
00:39:53,160 --> 00:39:55,920
on the CCTV from two weeks ago.

696
00:39:56,000 --> 00:39:57,920
We traced the route

697
00:39:58,000 --> 00:40:00,120
and found the car in the mountains.

698
00:40:00,200 --> 00:40:02,160
We also found blood in the car

699
00:40:02,240 --> 00:40:03,360
and this small wheel,

700
00:40:03,440 --> 00:40:05,600
which we suspect came off a suitcase.

701
00:40:05,680 --> 00:40:06,880
According to the hematology test,

702
00:40:06,960 --> 00:40:10,560
we confirmed it was Siu Zi-yiu's blood.

703
00:40:10,640 --> 00:40:14,800
Hold on...are you saying Sylvia
might have died two weeks ago?

704
00:40:14,920 --> 00:40:16,960
I'm sorry, who are you?

705
00:40:17,040 --> 00:40:18,480
I'm her ex-boyfriend.

706
00:40:18,560 --> 00:40:22,000
Kwan Sir...Mr. Yau said Siu Zi-yiu

707
00:40:22,080 --> 00:40:24,000
has been harassing him and his ex-wife
for the past two weeks.

708
00:40:24,080 --> 00:40:26,000
But he hasn't been able to find her.
